  "care.help.overview": "These component-based pages reproduce the supplied standalone designs using the authenticated demo API and CSV records.",
  "care.help.emergency": "Select a patient or create a temporary identity. Open the ED encounter, record triage, complete registration and care sections, then review disposition and handover before completion.",
  "care.help.inpatient": "Select a patient and admission source. Record the receiving team and coverage, reserve a compatible bed, verify the patient and admit. Continue in the nursing, medical, orders, transfer and discharge tabs.",
  "care.help.consultation": "Select a patient and consultation configuration. Use the section rail to complete the seven clinical sections. Save, preview and confirm before signing. Signed records accept addenda instead of edits.",
  "care.help.orders": "Version 2 adds structured medication, laboratory, imaging and procedure order dialogs. All entered order details are saved by the API. Cancellation retains the original order in history.",
  "care.help.preferences": "Effective theme, font scales, density, field presentation, language and date formats follow My Preferences and tenant locks. These pages do not add their own application sidebar.",
  "care.help.recovery": "Save draft writes an explicit API record. Restore uses the saved-record selector. Failed requests preserve entered values; retry keeps the same operation ID. Reload after a conflict replaces unsaved edits only after confirmation.",
  "care.help.boundary": "This is a reusable frontend demonstration, not a production clinical system. Payer verification, physical transfers, bed cleaning, real prescriptions and legally validated signatures require separate integrations. Do not enter real patient data.",
  "care.help.integration": "Inject createCareAdapter and the effective preference host into CareWorkspace. The authenticated POST /care-pages endpoint scopes saved records by tenant, application, user and page. Definitions and synthetic patients and beds come from backend JSON and CSV files.",
