  "designer.v1.removeRow": "Remove row",
  "designer.guide.contract.overview": "Compose reusable forms with shared controls, layouts, translations and rules. Designs and published answer examples use the demo API. Backend contract runtime demonstrates the supplied DCP v1 contract separately; the visual design is not a backend Dcp.Form payload.",
  "designer.guide.contract.workflow": "Add fields and sections, choose presentation and label language, and preview. Dropdowns can require up to four parents; map each child option to every parent. Import CSV/XLSX into a value set, review and save its revision. Save the design, select an owner type, review, approve and publish. Compare a saved release with the current design. Published forms load owner answers and show revision history.",
  "designer.guide.contract.validation": "Preview checks required values, types, ranges, normalization, calculations and dropdown membership. Any parent change clears dependent selections. The v1 runtime previews edits with server rules, supports repeating rows, and keeps false as a valid present Boolean value. A 422 response displays validation errors and does not confirm a save. A conflict or uncertain save requires reviewing the server record; writes are not automatically retried.",
  "designer.guide.contract.access": "Effective preferences and tenant locks still apply. Tenant-authored labels fall back from the selected language to English, then the original label. Shared recovery follows tenant retention and field exclusions and stores no browser-local copy. Recovery requires the same record revision and checksum. Draft Center lists DCP recovery drafts; open the designer and Backend contract runtime to review them. Masked and nonwritable v1 fields cannot be edited. Demo navigation and roles are not production field authorization.",
  "designer.guide.contract.integration": "Use DcpDesignerWorkspace for frontend authoring and DcpHostRuntime with createDcpRuntimeAdapter for host-bound v1 forms. The application supplies authenticated load, preview and save routes, scope identity and optional shared recovery scope. Revisions remain strings; collection rows use _id; omitted values retain data and null clears explicitly. Jira PLIBRYBEND-206 contains the verified backend handoff and remaining backend work. Advanced enterprise contracts and actual production/native acceptance are not yet complete.",
  "designer.guide.contract.controls": "The examples include RadioGroup, RangeField and FormErrorSummary. RangeField combines a slider with numeric entry; disabling it disables both controls. Error summaries announce validation and can focus the matching field.",
  "designer.repeatable": "Repeat this section",
  "designer.minItems": "Minimum rows",
  "designer.maxItems": "Maximum rows",
  "designer.rowLimit": "Add or remove rows to meet this section’s limits.",
  "designer.guide.contract.repeating": "Select a section and enable Repeat this section to add a bounded group of rows. Set minimum and maximum rows. Each row retains its own identity, values and validation messages. Calculations run per row; changing a shared parent clears dependent selections in every row. Copying a sample remaps its internal field references. Designer repetition currently supports one row level; nested collections are available in the separate v1 runtime.",
