  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.71d49e85599d": "GL reconciliation",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.2f4dcf59ff0c": "Exports",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.8584e6cbf061": "Approvals inbox",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.0183c8f4c882": "Workflow worklist",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.1b451b10ab6a": "Assistance",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.25e72b43612b": "Front office",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.a61759020289": "Front",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.1e2db1c3e418": "Coverage, authorization, estimates, deposits and the cash drawer.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.3109ee068fd2": "Today across every queue.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.c5a99c3f7444": "Verify each patient’s insurance before services are billed. Unverified coverage cannot be used for claims.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.7db701a6f095": "Request and track prior authorization. A partial approval records the approved amount for the claim.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.d358c1a8fb31": "Real-time eligibility against the payer. Results come from the simulator in this environment.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.ae3332164236": "Give patients a cost estimate and clear admission once the required deposit is held. Overrides need a second person.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.a44d70d529b7": "Money held against an encounter. Apply it to invoices, or request a transfer or refund for a second person to approve.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.d67f6576c5b6": "Open and close cashier drawers. Variances beyond the tolerance go to a supervisor for review.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.a0b1fabb0435": "Charges and documents",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.d3f9533d4d14": "Charges",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.6f3b0c575cc9": "From captured charge to issued invoice and its notes.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.f2445a83ad5e": "Encounters with charges not yet invoiced. Mark ready, hold with a reason, or create the invoice draft from priced charges.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.ba495e73ed65": "Every captured charge line. Price from the catalogue, reprice with a reason, send to review or reverse.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.035f831e442f": "Fees that no clinical order produces. Each needs approval by a second person before it becomes a charge.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.7b67d7e132d0": "Draft invoices are issued by someone other than the person who drafted them. Issued invoices never change; corrections use notes.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.a55782541937": "Increase what is owed on an issued invoice, for example a late charge. Issued by a second person.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.a4de0468a294": "Reduce what is owed on an issued invoice. Never more than the open balance; approved by a second person.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.8951c73f663b": "Contractual allowances, small-balance and bad-debt write-offs. Every write-off is decided by a second person.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.5ccc2e8715d7": "Money",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.2acbbe460866": "Receipts, allocation, refunds and prepaid packages.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.253c93d35c54": "Record money received and allocate it to open invoices. Voids need a second person and only apply to unallocated receipts.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.d05b6124a3da": "Approve refunds, dispatch them to the payout provider and confirm the outcome. The simulator never moves real money.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.b761886f2227": "Prepaid service packages. Record sessions as they are used; cancelling refunds the unused share less the fee.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.4594b737568a": "Insurance",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.b9238ed615fc": "Claims, exchange, remittances, appeals and payer balances.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.8effdc92c561": "Every payer claim from ready to paid. Submission through the exchange creates a tracked message.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.bb8e7075489f": "Live view of messages to and from payers. Retry failures or resolve them manually with a reason.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.1bc32031675c": "Payer remittance advice. Posting updates every claim and invoice it covers, so it is checked by a second person.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.221c1b99b77d": "Correct a keying or payer error on a posted remittance line. The difference is applied to the invoice on approval.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.47cbe0f431cd": "Contest denials before the filing deadline. Filing is approved by a second person; outcomes record what was recovered.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.b82910039655": "Compare what each payer should have paid with what arrived, period by period. Sign-off is independent.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.a61ef47d9a23": "Move a balance between payer levels or to the patient. Approval moves the money and bills the new party.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.29bab7b0a974": "Receivables",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.b1b7afa76db2": "AR",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.58fcbc6d8a75": "Aging, plans, statements, collections and reporting.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.cd00bef39de1": "Open balances by age and party.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.6b3d0a61b524": "Instalment agreements for patient balances. Approval generates the schedule; payments reduce it in order.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.406b1e2868e3": "Patient statements generated each cycle. Send them, record returned mail, or suppress for a reason.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.1afcef3bd66d": "Overdue patient balances move through reminders to a final notice. Agency referral needs a second person.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.6fd2a275ad2a": "Revenue cycle performance.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.b63474f0aafb": "Coding and models",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.a18b4be8e318": "Coding",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.4070d83cf384": "Coding, clinical clarification, grouping and model settlements.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.90636891ea9e": "Assign diagnosis and procedure codes. Coding is validated by a second coder before billing uses it.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.1a38884878e5": "Clinical documentation questions to clinicians. Answers return to the coder; unanswered queries escalate.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.076b053bbad9": "Run the licensed grouper on coded inpatient stays and validate the result before claims use it.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.af60090256bb": "Determine the visit level from medical decision making or time. A second person confirms or overrides it.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.6426d87573e3": "Capitation, bundle, budget and performance settlements per contract period, posted to the ledger after approval.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.ab48fcf706cb": "Accounting",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.ee69eb4afc76": "Ledger",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.ad9bd4c15cc5": "Journals, exceptions, reconciliation and ERP exports.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.26946f6bc76e": "Balanced journals produced by billing events. Missing GL mappings stop posting and appear here as exceptions.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.6e8f18e4c816": "Match subledger balances to the general ledger for each control account and period.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.e00e55777f03": "Batches of posted journals for the ERP. Each batch is approved before export and carries a checksum.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.40da9eca3031": "Cross-cutting",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.5985039f106d": "Team",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.5fd0fc3e0c99": "Approvals, workflow tasks and assistance suggestions.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.769bbbc4aa1d": "Everything waiting for a second person.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.d50857b66ae7": "Checkpoint tasks from claim, appeal, coding and collection workflows. Pick one up, block it with a reason, or finish it.",
  "ui.reference.rcm.definition.888ad8025f6d": "Suggestions from operational assistance. They never change records; a person accepts or dismisses each one.",
